      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242980",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/d0/d0f2ad53e20d7a679830054973c0592ae037e9cd01ea2a103c647cea807c6692.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $l$ and $m$ are two intersecting lines, and $m\u22201 = m\u22202$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$l$ and $m$ are perpendicular lines.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $m\u22201 = m\u22202$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\u22201$ and $\u22202$ are supplementary | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $m\u22201 + m\u22202 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u22202 + m\u22202 = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $m\u22202 = 90^{\u2218}$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $l$ and $m$ are perpendicular lines | {{field-6}} |"
    },
